                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9e186423-e00a-3833-9e2d-9239bd8d8f45",
                        "entry_id": "8f3e6a10-46ed-318f-8a2b-fe80a85c47d3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Something distasteful or physically unpleasant to touch."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "725b03b8-c829-4de9-89b4-696ea3d9e4f3",
                                "sense_id": "9e186423-e00a-3833-9e2d-9239bd8d8f45",
                                "text": "Like it wasn't bad enough that I was soaked to the bone, now I had to lug an ick covered designer original across a puddle filled runway."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "85ada6b6-d02d-4496-b789-3de2f3085dcf",
                                "sense_id": "9e186423-e00a-3833-9e2d-9239bd8d8f45",
                                "text": "The UN, for its part, has suggested eating insects as a way of feeding those extra mouths, which may put the frankenmeat ick factor in perspective."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f214dc6-c929-45ef-bd52-0bacfce34d89",
                                "sense_id": "9e186423-e00a-3833-9e2d-9239bd8d8f45",
                                "text": "Did you get ick all over my things? Should I walk myself through a car wash on the way home?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "af8d85e3-14b2-3821-ac29-01f092713103",
                        "entry_id": "8f3e6a10-46ed-318f-8a2b-fe80a85c47d3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A feeling of revulsion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "informal",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "628828c8-f18b-46d9-af45-c6c8f05fae3b",
                                "sense_id": "af8d85e3-14b2-3821-ac29-01f092713103",
                                "text": "to have the ick"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9868d510-f3c0-4431-8b90-8d639f71fe51",
                                "sense_id": "af8d85e3-14b2-3821-ac29-01f092713103",
                                "text": "And I was nodding, \"Uh-huh,\" trying not to have an ick attack, worrying, Is my face giving something away?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "34157d83-d85c-4e17-bf60-1096499ba00a",
                                "sense_id": "af8d85e3-14b2-3821-ac29-01f092713103",
                                "text": "I wish none of this bothered me, but I feel this ick about Burnham and it isn't going away."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7429aa2f-8ce9-4196-bd05-38e9d5e9ddf8",
                                "sense_id": "af8d85e3-14b2-3821-ac29-01f092713103",
                                "text": "She'd woken up today with a general ick about doing this job, but every time she considered canceling and giving Hailey her money back, she couldn't do it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e6fe6e4-75b7-435d-9c19-a9602972a6c1",
                                "sense_id": "af8d85e3-14b2-3821-ac29-01f092713103",
                                "text": "And as sad as that can be, we can't fake our feelings – if you've got the ick, you've got the ick."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b190aac-dc73-43b3-aa51-c923648de9a6",
                                "sense_id": "af8d85e3-14b2-3821-ac29-01f092713103",
                                "text": "“People use dating apps, but I don’t know anyone who pays for it,” Ms. Wang said. In fact, she said that she would consider it an “ick” if she learned somebody was paying for a subscription."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d9e15201-9d96-340e-ab3c-94c341b12c6b",
                        "entry_id": "8f3e6a10-46ed-318f-8a2b-fe80a85c47d3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Anything moaned about; a gripe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "slang",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "46943ea9-42ce-4fc3-b5f7-cfd15e46510a",
                                "sense_id": "d9e15201-9d96-340e-ab3c-94c341b12c6b",
                                "text": "How can you stand such an ick ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8fe4c4c-ed4d-43d2-842c-94914f1fb23d",
                                "sense_id": "d9e15201-9d96-340e-ab3c-94c341b12c6b",
                                "text": "Of course, the idea of drinking blood is a total ick right now, but I suppose once you—"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98de3143-a151-43b4-94c8-b11e1641e1d4",
                                "sense_id": "d9e15201-9d96-340e-ab3c-94c341b12c6b",
                                "text": "For the umpteenth time that day one of my fellow men regarded me with scorn. “You're so icky. Such an ick.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "43204010-20e9-4a8d-9a3d-267c07e34fef",
                                "sense_id": "d9e15201-9d96-340e-ab3c-94c341b12c6b",
                                "text": "I keep thinking back to last Valentine's Day—I was such an ick—and you sent me that card."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ccbd5710-66c3-44fe-9662-9ef217543e4a",
                                "sense_id": "d9e15201-9d96-340e-ab3c-94c341b12c6b",
                                "text": "The thought of him and his obsessive begging for sex gave me a predatory vibe and was a total ick."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
